Subject: Argument staging uses an incremental index

What this does
  Argument staging uses an incremental index.

Why we need it
  So lowering a large function (pdf.js) was quadratic in the IR size and encode-time bound.

What it adds
  `JSRegIR` gains `aw_def` (last destination write per value), `aw_reads` (non-destination read count) and `aw_last_win`, folded lazily by `regvm_arg_index_sync` as instructions are appended; `regvm_arg_retarget` makes the per-argument test O, `regvm_arg_retarget_insn` records the six call lowerings that retarget a producer into the call window, and a value outside the index falls back to the original `regvm_arg_retarget_scan` (`QJS_REGVM_ARGCHECK` cross-checks the two).

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
